# Displacement-product bounds in the ninth lift's pure kernel

The seven possible kernel masks from `ninth_pure_kernel_mask` have pairwise
product-displacement rank at most sixteen. There are only eight distinct
product matrices, including zero. Each is factored through an explicit
sixteen-row space. This separates every such pair from the native pair,
whose certified rank is twenty.

Changing the two generators of a kernel four-group preserves the displacement
product. Thus seven concrete products suffice for all distinct pairs.
All matrix products and row expansions are kernel checked. The native ATLAS
basis and packed-row convention are inherited from `KernelCount` and
`GeneratorCertificates.Packed`; the source application is Kleidman--Wilson
(1988), Section 2.1, p.489, without a printed/native marking identification.
-/
